From 9f37f3cfc793a67b3bfeb347f0226a6bffedeb99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 10:11:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: stm32: set system-clock-direction-out on stm32mp15
 mclk-fs links

'commit 5725bce709db ("ASoC: simple-card-utils:
Unify clock direction by clk_direction")'
introduced a change in sysclk direction management.

On STM32MP15 audio graph links using mclk-fs, the CPU DAI must advertise
MCLK output direction so ASoC calls set_sysclk() with CLOCK_OUT.
Without this property some links keep CLOCK_IN as default, which can
lead to invalid master clock configuration and wrong divider settings.

system-clock-direction-out is only relevant when the SAI or I2S instance
is the MCLK provider (#clock-cells set, master clock output). In that
case the direction must be CLOCK_OUT so that set_sysclk() programs and
enables the SAI/I2S master clock.

For SAI or I2S nodes that are not MCLK providers (MCLK consumer or no
master clock output), mclk-fs may still be present in the endpoint: it
is consumed by the machine driver (audio-graph-card) to compute the
MCLK frequency (rate x mclk-fs) and to configure the codec through
set_sysclk(). In this case system-clock-direction-out is not needed:
the SAI/I2S keeps the default CLOCK_IN direction and its set_sysclk()
does not drive any master clock. Adding it would wrongly request
CLOCK_OUT and could conflict with the actual MCLK provider.

Add system-clock-direction-out only to STM32MP endpoints whose SAI or
I2S instance is the MCLK provider.

Change-Id: I3f51a4ee03f6f41109b23fa53fad97349f3ee96d
Signed-off-by: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
